LumenHEIF changes
=================

1.2 (5 November 2026): MIME types

- Its Plugin file gives the MIME types it reads (image/heic, image/heif,
  image/avif), so Lumen 0.0.38 and later know HEIF and AVIF files by the
  filetypes MimeMap gives those, and can open them with a double-click.

1.1 (4 November 2026): the first release

- HEIF photos (.heic, .heif, .hif), as iPhones and many other phones take
  them, with libheif 1.23.7 and FFmpeg 5.1.10 cut down to its HEVC
  decoder.
- AVIF photos (.avif), with dav1d 1.5.4 for AV1, with riscos-ffmpeg's
  RISC OS changes. (1.1: AVIF was added after 1.0 was first built.)
- Built for ARMv7 with VFPv3; FFmpeg's and dav1d's NEON code is used
  where the processor has it, with exactly the same pictures either way.
- The photo's own thumbnail is used when it has one; Display P3 photos
  are converted to sRGB; sideways photos are turned the right way up.
- Each photo's encoding (HEVC or AV1, bits a channel, chroma, tiles) for
  Lumen's Info tab, and HEIF and AVIF named as separate formats.
- The EXIF is found wherever the file keeps it (Samsung phones write it
  after the picture data), so Lumen's Info tab lists it.
- A format plug-in (Lumen's plug-in API 1): it needs Lumen 0.0.37 or
  later.
- The LumenHEIF User Guide, in Guide. Its photos are samples from
  heic.digital and aviftools.net, not the author's.
- LumenHEIF-1.2-sources.zip has LumenHEIF's, libheif's, FFmpeg's and
  dav1d's sources and the patches, as the LGPL asks.
